# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots influxd (1.7.5, vulnerable to CVE-2019-20933) with
# an empty JWT shared-secret, creates the `admin` account the forged token
# targets, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING (with the empty shared-secret held in
#     memory) when the agent starts, which is what makes the "fixed the config
#     but never restarted the service" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting influxd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART influxd after setting a
# non-empty shared-secret, not merely edit the config - the live daemon keeps
# accepting empty-key JWTs until it is restarted.
